result: ''
description: 'The Vec/Map/String builtin method tables consulted by the typer and
  codegen must be the same table, so typer/codegen drift (the shift/first/last bug)
  becomes impossible. Introduce a shared enum BuiltinMethod (or shared descriptor
  table) that both passes match on exhaustively, or make codegen-completeness a compile-time-checked
  exhaustiveness over the typer''s set. Definition of done: a single shared registry
  of builtin methods (name, receiver type, signature) referenced by both typer and
  codegen; adding a method in one place forces the other; tests still green.'
